The day before the events at Mulan Hunting Ground.

103
10:54.510 --> 10:54.870
[Divine Constable, Qingyang]

104
11:46.630 --> 11:48.080
That is the God of Lies,

105
11:48.360 --> 11:49.150
Qipi.

106
11:50.150 --> 11:51.720
It has no eyes or nose,

107
11:51.800 --> 11:53.730
[God of Lies, Qipi]

108
11:52.240 --> 11:54.240
only a mouth that distorts the truth

109
11:54.510 --> 11:56.240
and deceives people's hearts.

110
11:59.440 --> 12:00.510
Chief.

111
12:02.080 --> 12:03.270
Why are you here?

112
12:03.750 --> 12:05.200
It's almost midnight.

113
12:05.270 --> 12:06.670
You were in there for a long time,

114
12:06.670 --> 12:08.670
so I thought I'd come and take a look.

115
12:09.910 --> 12:11.670
As expected, nothing escapes

116
12:11.910 --> 12:13.390
the Chief's eyes.

117
12:15.840 --> 12:18.550
Tianshu Pavilion is really too big.

118
12:18.630 --> 12:21.030
I accidentally lost track of time.

119
12:23.720 --> 12:25.270
To linger like this,

120
12:26.080 --> 12:27.790
you must have found something

121
12:27.840 --> 12:29.510
interesting to you.

122
12:33.960 --> 12:35.420
I originally thought that

123
12:35.550 --> 12:36.590
Tianshu Pavilion

124
12:36.720 --> 12:38.630
was only used to store archives.

125
12:38.870 --> 12:39.870
I didn't expect

126
12:40.910 --> 12:41.720
there to be

127
12:41.720 --> 12:43.450
such a magnificent place here.

128
12:44.240 --> 12:45.910
I am but a layman.

129
12:46.080 --> 12:47.510
Despite studying them for a long while,

130
12:47.510 --> 12:49.040
I still couldn't figure out

131
12:49.270 --> 12:50.630
what was so profound

132
12:50.720 --> 12:52.360
about these god murals.

133
12:52.840 --> 12:54.840
If, as the Chief just said,

134
12:55.630 --> 12:57.550
Qipi represents lies,

135
12:58.320 --> 12:59.120
then

136
12:59.150 --> 13:00.790
what do the other gods

137
13:01.360 --> 13:02.720
represent?

138
13:03.550 --> 13:04.720
Chief,

139
13:05.150 --> 13:07.870
could you please enlighten me?

140
13:12.030 --> 13:13.080
This is Kelu,

141
13:13.670 --> 13:15.630
and this is Rangnan.

142
13:16.070 --> 13:19.750
They respectively oversee the Immortality and Prophecy of all beings.

143
13:19.750 --> 13:20.550
Kelu?

144
13:21.870 --> 13:23.480
Is it the God Kelu that Wen Nansheng

145
13:23.480 --> 13:24.480
mentioned?

146
13:25.630 --> 13:26.440
Qipi

147
13:27.960 --> 13:29.200
represents lies.

148
13:31.080 --> 13:34.240
Haiqu is in charge of hatred.

149
13:34.100 --> 13:35.360
[God of Hatred, Haiqu]

150
13:36.030 --> 13:38.080
Qiuyu is the God of Calamity.

151
13:36.370 --> 13:38.330
[God of Calamity, Qiuyu]

152
13:38.870 --> 13:40.390
And this last one,

153
13:41.240 --> 13:42.080
Hanluo,

154
13:43.360 --> 13:45.910
represents death.

155
13:46.310 --> 13:49.050
[God of Death, Hanluo]

156
13:49.630 --> 13:51.270
Are these all murals

157
13:51.270 --> 13:52.730
of the ancient Liluo Sect?

158
13:53.630 --> 13:54.720
But why are they here

159
13:54.720 --> 13:56.920
in the secret room of Tianshu Pavilion?

160
13:58.150 --> 13:59.390
These murals

161
13:59.840 --> 14:01.600
look really strange.

162
14:02.360 --> 14:03.270
They really don't look like

163
14:03.270 --> 14:04.870
things from our Shi Dynasty.

164
14:05.240 --> 14:06.030
Chief,

165
14:06.480 --> 14:08.270
may I know why you kept them

166
14:08.670 --> 14:10.870
in the secret room of Tianshu Pavilion?

167
14:11.910 --> 14:12.910
These are indeed

168
14:13.440 --> 14:15.270
not products of our Shi Dynasty.

169
14:16.270 --> 14:17.720
The reason they are sealed in

170
14:17.720 --> 14:19.670
the deepest part of Tianshu Pavilion

171
14:19.670 --> 14:20.600
is that

172
14:22.320 --> 14:25.270
these things are highly ominous.

173
14:26.030 --> 14:26.910
Seeing them,

174
14:27.750 --> 14:28.960
you will understand

175
14:29.750 --> 14:30.960
where all the

176
14:30.960 --> 14:32.360
pain and sin in this world

177
14:33.240 --> 14:34.480
come from.

178
14:37.090 --> 14:38.280
Are these gods

179
14:38.960 --> 14:41.150
actually the source of all pain

180
14:42.080 --> 14:43.630
and sin in the world?

181
14:47.320 --> 14:48.380
You must remember.

182
14:49.720 --> 14:52.030
Even the closest people around you

183
14:52.910 --> 14:54.600
may not be what you see

184
14:55.080 --> 14:56.550
with your own eyes.

185
15:02.240 --> 15:04.570
I will keep the Chief's teachings in mind.

186
15:27.580 --> 15:30.910
[Yeqiao Town, Outskirts of Tianhuang City]

187
16:30.000 --> 16:30.790
Miss.

188
16:31.030 --> 16:32.470
It's hot. Have some herbal tea.

189
16:32.470 --> 16:33.150
Take a look.

190
16:34.510 --> 16:35.510
It cools you down.

191
16:35.670 --> 16:36.480
Aunt Wang.

192
16:36.930 --> 16:37.910
Did you just make this?

193
16:37.910 --> 16:39.840
Yes, it's freshly woven.

194
16:40.120 --> 16:41.080
Excuse me, sir.

195
16:41.550 --> 16:42.870
May I ask

196
16:43.270 --> 16:45.080
